"Ever notice how a smell can dredge up some of the craziest or strangest of memories? I have read before that odour memory falls off less rapidly than any other sensory memory such as taste, or touch. perfume companies make millions a year because of our sense of smell. I know I am not the only one that will pass by someone in a store, and have them remind me of an ex because of the same cologne being used. or the smell of someones hair on a pillow. As weird as this is, the smell of morning breath, sometimes not being entirely pleasant, however, there is something comfortable in someones morning breath,someone you love. Turning over in the morning, feeling that warmth against your cheek, and inhaling that musky deep scent as it dances on your face. Everyone has their own scent. enough of that. In these futile days of hopeless attitudes, beaten dreams, and greedy hearts, in these days when no one asks why and just goes with whatever, in order to save time or save effort, I feel lost. I feel misplaced. Why? Because I refuse to believe this is as good as it is going to get. That this is as good as i will get, or my life as a whole, or this world as a whole. I refuse to believe that my actions or presense here has no effect on anything or anyone around me because I am not everything I had once thought I would be. There is a darkness around us now. A haze that has trapped us in this pudding like pool of hopelessness and defeat. People settle for the easiest choices. Once more I will state this...EASY IS NOT ALWAYS BETTER!!!!! So what if I am the living definition of overly sensitive and emotional. I feel things others don't seem to. I see that person sitting at their desk, thinking no one notices the downcast eyebrows, or the worry running rampant in their eyes. I feel their grief, their anxiety, their troubled hearts. Maybe it is just me thinking of how I feel when I look like that, I have the worst poker face in the world. Yet I feel in tune with every emotion everyone feels. I feel that sadness, i feel sad when i feel that persons hatred or anger. I feel when someone is in love, and I even get jealous of that. I wish sometimes I had a shield I could put up so that those emotions didnt swarm to me and fill me with everyone elses troubles. But that is who I am. Because of that I am able to be there for others, to be able to be honestly caring and empathetic to everyones needs. Next time you are around someone take the moment to really look at them. really look at someone next time you do something for them or say something to them. remember that they are a person and have their own thoughts and feelings, and you have an impact, even if it is small, on their day. and it spirals from there. Do you want to impact the world in a good or bad way? it all starts with what you do or say to that one person. Some think I am too nice, and yes, maybe in the world we live in now, i would be considered too polite and nice, but hey, I believe that I was put here to stand for the truth and give the love that is in me, that feels so often as though it will swallow me whole because I cant get it out enough.I feel that somehow this crazy disease i have of loving too much and feeling too much will bring light through this darkness around us now and enlighten the path for many people to that place where hope is found. next subject isnt it odd how some of the smartest people are idiots. a person could have graduated top of their class from harvard, yet be the biggest idiot you will ever meet because of their actions toward others. random thought time:) too many realizations today about how i have treated things and allowed myself to get caught up with things that were obvious to everyone but me that they were not what I had planned them to be and that I was the only one still caught up in it all. too long a story to get into, but some words of advice. sometimes you have to bite the bullet and let go. figure out if it is the fantasy you are holding on to or something real that can and will happen. I can honestly say there is only one person in this world that I think I have not brought good into their lives. I feel that I have brought something good to others and made their lives somewhat better, only one person does it seem like that wasnt affected positively, or at least wont admit to it, and I think that is why it has been so hard for me to be ok with how things are between us. it is not the best feeling knowing that someone seems more unhappy because you were in their life. I dont know why or what it was. see, i am the kind of person that is the same with everyone. sometimes some people will act differently with others, I am the same me with everyone, silly, sweet, fun, honest, totally me. and i think that bothers some people, bothers them because they cant be that way. some people are like bad chocolate cake. you first taste the sweet icing, wonderful, tasty, but you get to the inside after savoring the frosting and you find it to be dry, crumbly, and sour, and you try to eat bites of it with frosting, yet the sourness still surfaces and makes you gag. some people are different. some have less than yummy icing but after that they have sweet, moist cake inside that makes you forget that the icing was dry and flaky. blah blah blah right:) enough for now. a war is going on inside me. ever have that inside voice scream to you ""what are you doing"" ""why are you doing this"" ""this isnt how it has to be"" well...mine does it more than ever lately.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3570245.female.24.indUnk.Taurus,,,,,,0
"Hello to all, Well the only way i can effectively begin my blog is by first saying my amazing adventure of the flights. As some people know i left home at 7:00 AM. Mind you my flight was not scheduled to leave until nine AM. When i get there i find out that my flight has been canceled because of a shortage of the crew, which was what i found out through my friend's mother: stella, who is one of the best and kindest people in this world. We were on standby, which means that if there was room in one of the later flights i would get in. My friends' Marlene and Dalia were in the same dilema. there were four available seats in the eleven o clock flight, there was no room in the ten oclock flight. THe only plus side to the ten oclock flight was that I met the Mayor of chicago and took a picture with him, actually Marlene is in the picture also. Anyway people who had paid for the eleven oclock flight came which left only two available seats in that flight. Unfortinately because of the way the alphabet is i was unable to go so both my friends went. I did not feel bad because luckily thanks to my papi and my cousin David i had my laptop in my bookbag. Therefore i played minesweeper until the battery went out which was around the time when the twelve-fifty flight left. Me being the one who was already close to two hours later than both my friends, had to go through a lot of paperwork and was unable to go to my room, to which i lost my swipe card to by the way, so i could not enter the dorm building. Which was great all on it's own. by the time i took all my bags to the fourth floor, to where my room was, i was hungry-verrrryyyyy hungry- so we decided to go out and eat, there is a chinese place here that makes the best shrimp fried rice. I dont think i can take some over there but i think that i can give it a try. Anyways my friend Dalia and i were surprised to find out that a the person i was sharing my bathroom with, was indeed a BOY. Exactly imagine how i felt. I slept in my friends bed that night because i thought it creepy to sleep in a room next to a boy who had total access to my bedroom not to mention my bathroom, Yiuuuckkkk. This was how my firts day was, eventhough i went through a lot i got to meet a lot of people who live in my ""appartment building"" For your information i changed my bedroom location the very next day at eleven in the morning and also got a new swipe card in order to actually get in and out of the building. I hope that helps you sleep better. La version en Castellano... De Chicago a Boston Hola a todos... bueno al única manera que efectivamente puedo empezar mi “BLOG” es contando de mi maravillosa aventura de mi vuelo. Como algunos saben deje casa a la 7:00 AM. Advertido que el vuelo no estaba programado para salir hasta las 9:00. Para cuando llegue a ahí me entere que mi vuelo había sido cancelado debido a una ausencia de pilotos, lo cual supe a través de la mama de mi amiga Marlene: Stella, quien es una de las bondadosas y buena persona de este mundo. Nos dejaron en “STANDBY” lo cual significa que si es que hay espacio en uno de los vuelos posteriores nos admiten. Mis amigas Marlene y Dalia estaban en el mismo dilema. Había cuatro sitios disponibles en el vuelo de las 11, y ya no había sitio en el vuelo de las 10. Lo único bueno del vuelo de las 10 fue que conocí al Alcalde de Chicago y me tome una foto con él, actualmente Marlene esta en la foto también. De cualquier manera, gente que había pagado por el vuelo de las once llegaron y solo quedaban dos sitios disponibles. Desdichadamente por razón del alfabeto yo no pude tomar ese vuelo así que mis amigas se fueron. No me sentí mal por mi suerte pues gracias a mi papi y mi primo David tenia mi Laptop en mi bolsa de mano. Así que me quede jugando “MINESWEEPER” hasta que la batería se acabo, que fue cuando el vuelo de las 12:50 salía. Siendo la única que era ya mas de dos horas tarde después de mis amigas, tuve que pasar por un montón de documentación y no pude llegar a mi dormitorio, pues hasta perdí la tarjeta de ingreso al edificio. Lo cual fue magnifico por si mismo, pues para cuando llegue con todas mis maletas al cuarto piso, donde queda mi cuarto, estaba hambrienta- súper hambrientaaaaaaaaaaaaa- asi que decidimos ir a comer afuera, hay este sitio de comida china que vende el mejor arroz chaufa de camarones. No se si pueda llevar algo de regreso mas tratare. De cualquier manera dalia y yo nos sorprendimos que la persona que compartía mi cuarto , era efectivamente un HOMBRE. Exactamente, imagínense como me senti. Dormí en la cama de mi amiga por que pensé que era muy dormir en el cuarto junto a un muchacho que tenia total acceso a mi dormitorio y sin contar mi baño. Yiuuuckkk. Así fue como paso mi primer día, a pesar de todo lo que pase pude conocer a un monton de gente que vive en mi edificio comunal. Para tu información cambie mi cuarto al mañana siguiente a las once de la mañana, y tambien consegui otra tarjeta de acceso para salir y entrar al edificio. Espero esto te ayude a dormir mejor.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3809513.female.17.indUnk.Taurus,,,,,,0
