"So, it's around 2:00 am and I am awake on my computer. Why? You may ask. Why, when you have to be at school at 7 o freakin clock in the morning? Well, let me explain. Reason # 1) Recently, my sleeping schedule and patterns have become highly irregular and spastic. And there is nothing I can do to control it. Before Spring Break, I had been going to bed at midnight every night and getting a healthy five hours of sleep. After Spring Break, I fall asleep around 9, wake up at 11, fall back asleep at midnight, wake up again at 3 am, and force myself back to sleep until around 5:30. Reason # 2) Today, it was more spastic than ever. I fell asleep around 7, woke up at 9, fell back asleep, woke up at 11. fell back asleep, woke back up around midnight and realized that Hey! My To Kill A Mockingbird essay is due tomorrow and I have not even written the intro or conclusion for it! So, I dragged myself out of bed, opened up a diet snapple, and started typing. Well, now that is done and I still have some math homework to do. But amazingly I am no longer tired. I don't know if it is because of the five hours or so of sleep I got earlier, but I know this is not healthy in the long run. Maybe I need to see a doctor. Reason # 3) I tend to think a lot when I am by myself. Part of the reason I am not tired anymore is because once I started typing my essay I started thinking about what life would be like if I went to TAMS next year and how I would find out that my writing really sucks and how I suck at transitions within my essay (as demonstrated by the judges at the district meet who wrote about my paper, ""Your paper is very unclear. I lost track of what side you were on, as it seemed to shift many times...your paragraph transitions added to the confusion, and your lack of focus made the paper hard to read."" and yet I got 4th place...what are these people thinking??) and I thought about that guy I wrote about long ago...the one at lunch, remember? Yeah him, the intriguing one...well, he sits with me and my group of people now instead of the other group that sits down the table from us because they kind of just stopped making room for him (sad I know). He helped me study today for my history test and was very amusing, as well as helpful. He also retains a myriad of useless facts...I found it quite interesting. I am getting off the subject...so...whenever I started typing, I started thinking, and now I am wide awake Reason # 4) Even if I tried to, I wouldn't be able to go back to sleep. I have reached this conclusion after nights of laying in bed for hours on end, counting sheep, slowing down my breathing, trying to clear my mind...only after three hours am I able to somehow force myself to drift to sleep and if I did that now it would be useless because I would be waking up two minutes after falling asleep. Do you see my predicament? I have insomnia. I need to see a doctor. So basically, that is all I have to write about. Because I have no life. Oh yeah, I was gonna turn in an application to McDonalds today (because they are hiring!) but then I fell asleep before my mom got home with the car. I need a car. That guy has close to $10,000 saved up for a car because he worked two jobs this summer full time and is also working close to full time now (or at least I think that is what he said). He also turns 17 next week but can't get his license because he says his parents hate him. I hope no one reads this that will know who I am talking about. Well, gtg. Lisa ""Only two things are infinite- the universe and human stupidity- and I'm not sure about the former."" -Albert Einstein",0,normal,blog_corpus,1234631.female.17.indUnk.Aquarius,,,,,,0
