"How many days left?! I'm not even going to get into the shopping days that are left. I never shop for Christmas until the 24th anyway. The holiday spirit just doesn't descend upon me until then. But it is beginning to look a lot like Christmas around here. We're making holiday cards this year - an old-fashioned Christmas; and we're baking all of our gifts. Mini pumpkin pies, sugar drop cookies, pumpkin bread and the best chocolate chip cookies I've ever tasted. And they ship well, too. Last night we decided (we being my two children) that it was time to decorate the tree. Only problem is that we don't have a tree. Got lost in all the moving over the past 3 years, I guess. So, I suggested we decorate the bamboo tree on the terrace. They loved it! And after we were finished with the tree (we being mostly me this time), it looked pretty good. Why shouldn't you have a bamboo tree for Christmas in Miami? We are the epitomy of tropical chic. *grin* And, if it had been 40 degrees colder last night, it would have snowed. At 74 degrees, what we got was rain. Truly a tropical Miami Christmas *sigh* Diva out.",0,normal,blog_corpus,766556.female.34.indUnk.Sagittarius,,,,,,0
