"Wowsers, I just tried transferring my Blogspot journal over to LiveJournal, what an ordeal, YA RIGHT!&nbsp; I'm happy here, why the hell not stay here huh?&nbsp; LOL... &nbsp; Well, I'm not sure what the last entry was, or what it was, but I really need to keep on that ball.&nbsp; I'm in my Masters Program, I've been debating well for the better part of a month on whether I actually want to go back or not... I DO!&nbsp; It is was I see myself doing. &nbsp; I've been absolutely terrified about monetary issues...&nbsp; Can I afford to go back?&nbsp; I guess so... Can I stand living under the poverty line eating horrible second rate food that can't help but go to my hips... sure!&nbsp; Tom and I have decided that we're going to find someone who'll do 2-4-1 Emergency lipposuction, it's the only logical solution.&nbsp; &nbsp; Lots going on right now, this Friday Night shall be my first outing to a bar in a very long time... since that time with Mun and Ryan last summer to Armanis where I encountered Teenaged bitch girls with too much attitudes.&nbsp; &nbsp; I've also decided that Tom and Mark are stunting my creativity and my attempts at becoming a deeper person.&nbsp; Mark is totally superficial and Tom struggles at the best of times. &nbsp; Mark and I never talk about anything other than work, the weather and what we've done today.&nbsp; I want to know what he thinks about things, not what his friends think, not what his dad thinks, not what his professors think, his very own thoughts.&nbsp; He's always worried that his clothes aren't meeting GAP standards of 'lack-of-colour' and 'lack-of-creativity' to have a deep conversation.&nbsp; Does he think for himself?&nbsp; Or is her one of those typical over consuming north american can't think for themselves, let media decide persons? &nbsp; Well, it's gonna be eight months on the 29th, so I better start learning... &nbsp; On a brighter note, Tom and I had a fabulous dinner tonight, on the Hibatchi, it took not too long, infact, just enough time for me to run to meet my aunt and grandma to do ""The Cheque Thing"" which is (if I haven't mentioned it before online) they write me a cheque, I cash it and the go to BINGO.&nbsp; With the almost expected outcome of them being down $300 and the cheque bouncing out of my account disrupting my bill payments and my own personal life. &nbsp; Oh Well, that's family, and I suppose, in some strange way, I wouldn't have it any other way. &nbsp; Well, I'm going to go visit Tom downstairs, he's watching ABFAB all by his lonesome, before Jehny D comes over.&nbsp; I'm not sure if I've mentioned that either here, but Jehny D's moving back down south, we are having a farewell martini party here next saturday night. &nbsp; TTYL HUGS DAN &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",0,normal,blog_corpus,1328709.male.25.indUnk.Gemini,,,,,,0
