"ok so for one my friend dave asked me if I ever write about him in my blog and I sadi no......he seemed a littl disapointed. So here it is Dave your 15 min. Your in my blog. I think your awsome and I would totally make-out with you even thought you think I'm kidding when I ask you that repeatedly. ok so here the real reason for this blog entry. I'm addicted to 6 feet under. You know that HBO series. I don't have cable but DAVE owns the first season, and one day we were hanging out at his house we started to watch it....big mistake. I can't get enough and as soon as I start watching it it's really hard for me to stop. So everytime I go over there and he's like ok we can watch one episode....well it turns into like three.And the sad part is I never get bored. Sweet Jesus.........I could sit and watch it for hours. I could honsetly sit and watch the whole first season right through no breaks. I can't fathom having to wait a week to see the next episode!!! 3 hours of it just isn't long enough. I realized yesterday I love jesus jokes. well not jokes about jesus.....but like when ppl say things like ""sweet jesus"" that is some good fucking pie!!! you know what I mean.",0,normal,blog_corpus,2751885.female.24.indUnk.Pisces,,,,,,0
"...it's been an odd week. Maybe the blog reflects it, I am not sure. Here what's happening. Next week I am going up to Atlanta and will be going to Emory clinic. They have one of the country's best neurology departments. In case you are a reader who didn't know, I was diagnosed with Parkinson's Disease two or three years ago. My going to Emory is because a new neurologist I am seeing went to school there and would like me to get a work-up from them and then a recommendation on how to proceed with treatment. There is talk of possibly Doing Brain Surgery , and, in all honesty I am really scared of that happening. I mean this is the brain we are talking about here, you know? The central command...headquarters...where it all comes from. Anything goes wrong and I am screwed. There's something else. I am in denial of the illness in very real ways. I don't read much about it or seek information. I think that to do that fixates my mind on it and makes it real-er in some way. I don't communicate with others with Parkinson's (PD) because seeing others shows me what's in store for me. I'm not sure I can handle that just yet. But damn. I'm only 43 you know? This wasn't supposed to happen. At least not yet. I feel too young to be losing body functions like fine motor skills in my left hand. I'm too self-conscious a person to have a disease that makes me occasionally shake and I can't make it stop. I deal with enough inner shame in my life not to have my body adding to it, you know? Just too young to have my body already betraying me. I know... I know... it can be shown that there are plenty of people, even younger than me, far far worse off. I know that. But I gotta process this for me too. I need to work through how I deal with this. And yes, the ""why me"" thing needs to be brought up and dealt with. So it's been an odd week. Next week I need to acknowledge my dragon, and find answers on how to best deal with it. I'd really prefer not to go and can give you a long list of things that really need to be done instead of running up to town and losing a day. But I think the regret over not actively trying to find answers would outweigh the temporary hassle of making the trip up there. Sorry... no silliness in this entry. But I'll work on it and try to be more entertaining next time. Anyway. I'll keep you posted. Thanks for listening, okay?",0,normal,blog_corpus,3397827.male.43.indUnk.Scorpio,,,,,,0
