"Just to clarify my oil drilling stance: Democrats have all but successfully kept it off the Energy Bill for this session, but the bill is still being debated. Republicans conceded defeat on the oil issue, allowing them to move on to other topics in the bill. Wednesday’s big story was CIA Director George Tenet’s assertion that Saddam would not attack first. What made this big is that it seems a departure from Bush’s pre-emptive attack stance, yet Bush’s PR guy Ari Fleischer asserts that this is what Bush feels as well. I’ve been saying this since the beginning: What better reason to give Iraq for using their weapons than to instigate them? In the end, will Saddam probably have weapons to use on U.S. troops, most likely. And will their be deaths resulting from this? Most likely. But there are protocols and laws that have to be followed and that means going in with inspections first. Without laws and protocols there is anarchy, which isn't any better. I wanted to get into some other things, but working 60 hours a week doesn’t leave me with much time. There’s some stories from tonight’s paper I wanted to say something about, but we didn’t get off to the press (note the singular, my paper is NOT major) in time because of the breaking story with the latest death in the Washington, D.C. area sniper shootings. Today was also a horrible day on Wall Street and I’m convinced that everything I own stock will continue plummeting more than others, just because. I know sitting and waiting it out is the way to go, but Christ, do we really need to go this low? Tomorrow’s topic will cover race, and issue I haven’t gotten into here very much, but the story that I’m dealing with raises some serious issues that I can’t say were ever gone over in any of my many race classes at Temple. Of course, I wasn’t about to bring them up, I fall more to the Socialist (oh god, the FBI will be watching now) viewpoint and think race confuses the larger issue: class. With that can of worms open, good night! P.S. I'm not sure what the screw up is that immediately follows this paragraph, but I can't edit it. Somehow my edit link takes me to The New York Times link. Weird.",0,normal,blog_corpus,855133.male.25.Communications-Media.Cancer,,,,,,0
