"i’ve totally been undedicated to God lately. the thing i love most in the world, and i can’t even chase after it. i sure can chase after everything else materialistic and worldy. as ecclesiastes says, “a striving after the wind.” my whole life this week has been just that. and for the most part, many of the weeks before that. - Kevin's Blog I think it's so easy for us to fall into the path of materialism. Holding the posessions we have in such high honor, rather than understanding that they're not that important, they're things God has blessed us with. I've noticed in my life I tend to do this a bit, but not really that much. I'm pretty content with what I have, I think it comes from not really having that much. Sure, there are things that I would like, but really I'm content with what I have and I don't try to get them very much, and if I do and they're taken away, I'm upset for a bit but get over it (IE: Guitar that I don't get back till next month). However I notice just how much Americans as a whole are materialistic. Wealth and levels of achievement really all depend on how much you have, what you have, and how much it's ""worth"" (how you can put a worth on things that aren't important is beyond me). Americans seem to think that the way to happiness is through things... that's why if you notice, when Americans go overseas they try to give the people things in hopes that it will make them happier. Just something I'm pondering.",0,normal,blog_corpus,1031806.male.17.Technology.Sagittarius,,,,,,0
"Welcome to my blog, one of a gajillion bzillion on the net. What sets this one apart from the others? I am a different person. Funny how that works out, hunh? Here you will hear, or read, rather, my thoughts of any given situation or thing. Please don't take my opinions too seriously, but enjoy my ramblings. Take all you'll eat, but eat all you take. The sentence right before this one was a quote from a popular tv show. I will be doing that a lot here, since tv is a big influence on the way I live life and view the world. As a matter of fact, I will be going to a deserted island soon and a camera crew is following me for some reason. I have to survive using only my gut instinct, and some instructions written down by some girl who calls herself a ""Script Supervisor"", whatever that is. I will give you a heads up if I need to voice my serious opinions, along with an ""end rant"" to signify my steam has been vented. The internet is a tool created by Al Gore for the express purpose of spreading pornography to the eyes of the world. No, wait, the internet is for posting one's thoughts. Also for the viewing of funny home videos. Your comments about any given thought are more than welcome. Please keep comments free of any vulgarity. Questionable posts will be deleted. Thank you for your consideration. p.s. I was only kidding about the deserted island thing. Don't even get me started on the Al Gore nonsense!",0,normal,blog_corpus,3771338.male.27.Communications-Media.Leo,,,,,,0
