"""Do not go where the path may lead, Go instead where there is no path and leave a trail"" - Ralph Waldo Emerson I saw this statement somewhere, wrote down in a piece of paper and saved it. Yesterday going through some stuff I found it. I had put aside the plans to go to London for a while - actually for two years. I kinda decided to walk through others' path. Thought about getting settled. Moved on my own, bought furniture, kept the same job for over a year, made stable friends. Sounded like a plan! Consider this: For many in the US, moving from their parents' house and making on their own is a dream. The American dream. As a matter of fact, I am Brazilian. We live in our parents house for ever, unless we get married and move to somebodyelse's house. But I did it differently. I moved to the US without knowing anyone nor speaking any English. It was hard, scary sometimes. I made it though, with Jehovah's help, and I am proud of it after all. But I want more, I wanna leave a trail. Natal(Brazil)->New York->London->Wherever. But it's just a trail, my trail. No need to be followed. Leave your own!!!",0,normal,blog_corpus,3995290.female.27.Law.Capricorn,,,,,,0
