"the score to June sixth Rufus Wainwright's Want One. Beautiful, plainitive melodies and distinctly unamerican lyrics. A voice I could listen to for days and not tire of. Donnie Darko soundtrack. Strangely sad, amazingly beautiful. The sound of passing life. The cars that pass you on the road. The strangers that look at you on buses, glances you'll never see again. I'm floating again. Utterly displaced. I'm losing meaning. I missed the entire slipping process. I just looked and something was gone. The meaning of me, individually as a person, is out of my grasp right now, and I don't know where I ought to look. I had utterly isolated. My phone was silenced. My body was still. I felt the extent of feeling totally empty, constant restlessness, no core to go to, draw from.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3062752.female.27.Communications-Media.Taurus,,,,,,0
