"The weather is affecting me, but I still am on the rebound from an exceptionally wonderful Tuesday. I've been thinking about places I've been and the feelings they conjure up when I think of them. California San Jose and then Bakersfield?(San Fran area) - I remember it in two stages, once as my adolescent memory trips visions of dark nights with yellow sodium-powered street lamps and another as my adult mind really just wondering why anyone would want to live in California. I remember it being fast when I was young and when I was just recently in California it seemed like everyone was lost or searching. Missoula Montana - amazed, enchanted, and enthralled with that state. Beautiful mountains, interesting city-scapes and that feeling only sitting in a bar where people are trying to sell rifles and pistols while drunk to buy more liquor can only produce. People actually enjoying life, hitch hikers, hunters and drifters. Lots of hippies too. Texas - Dallas to be exact, large city of never ending shopping malls and parking lots. Deep Ellum is at least interesting for about 30 minutes, a whole 15 minutes longer than the rest of Dallas. Scott and James, good times were had and it makes me only wish we had longer. Mexico - Dirty, damned dirty, sometimes smelly. Only in the confines of the nice resort can I appreciate the weather, the beer at 10 AM and refried beans with every meal. Smelly-Cow cheese attributes to the smell. Although most of my thoughts are negative I will always remember the sun, sand, love, sea breeze, lazy, Jack Kerouac, Monster Garage, cheap smokes, sales people, bargaining, shopping. I hope now that I updated maybe Abe will too. I see that Amanda has her priorities straight...",0,normal,blog_corpus,445935.male.26.Agriculture.Pisces,,,,,,0
