"Hey Dan, and Everyone let's start that Debate blog . Let's start with something a on the lighter side before jumping into war talk, or race talk, something all deep and heavy like that. And let's try and avoid ""re-debating"" issues that have been/ are being debated to death. For instance no one is really interested in what band has sold out or hasn't. (all this use of the word debate is getting me....tired). And of course, let's try to remember; if you are arguing something that you are uninformed about, then there is no point in debating it. I'm not being facetious, I just mean the whole point of debating (well, what the point SHOULD be) is to take two informed, thought out sides and pit them against each other. Not in any Sophist way, where one side is just trying to win (i.e. make fallacious arguments to give only the appearance of making a point without actually making the point) but in a way that opens up all the perspective and really flushes out the ideas of each point. There is nothing against using the so called, devil's advocate, either to try and flush out ideas and weak spots (though often playing the devil's advocate is done merely to try and win)or to move the argument to each logical step. Remember this is not a competition, and we are trying to debate in the sense that a winning conclusion must be sought. How does anyone/everyone feel about this?",0,normal,blog_corpus,798653.male.26.indUnk.Aquarius,,,,,,0
