"One episode of ""deadwood"" nominated and it is the pilot?? Granted, I love the pilot. Got me in to the show, but that Ricky Jay Episode was the meaning of perfection in a one hour drama. Drunken monologue, love stories galore, flim-flammery, it had it all. 4 episodes of the sopranos? Horseshit. In should have been flipped like Adrianna (although good for Drea's nomination, she did a great job). Mind you, it is a good show, but as i've said time and time again, episode for episode, deadwood hands down beat up on the sopranos. no, not beat up, but killed slowly, with a saw and hatchet, piece by piece. David Chase was sitting in his mohagony chair this morning, in the terrycloth white robe the cast and crew got him for a wrap gift, watching the nominations for best writing in a dramatic series thnking to himself, ""Damnit, the only way i could have won is if they nominated anything but ""Deadwood"". I will lose, the house bets are on me, but damn it, i'm going to lose. I'll get you david milch, i'll get you good..."" Also, I might like to point out that Ian McShane got no nomination. Congrats to my new co-workers though, mr. garber and ms. garner. I guess any awards show that posthumously gives the ""modern day charlie chaplin"" a nod can't be that bad. There's still the golden globes I guess, the only real awards show left. yea, i said it, what?",0,normal,blog_corpus,3552574.male.24.Arts.Scorpio,,,,,,0
