"Well!! the world of computer tecnics in its varying languages and softwares is another world for a doctor. Yet it has become so familiar with time & need.I learnt a bit of one,then another then another and now yet another. This time I explore the world of HTML/XHTML/XML to get a clearer understanding of the language of the Blog and its design.It is a bit easier for me,just because I know how to use Frontpage editor,Photoshop quite comfortably and already have 3 published websites and one webpage. There was a time in school when I was quite well versed in BASIC,C and had ventured into UNIX before I took a turn that lead me into the world of body & disease mechanics. Now that I have experience in sticking people with needles,suturing up differnt forms of tissue,delivering babies,disease diagnosis, assisting varied operations,seeing patiens recover while seeing some die and also handle a few unforgettable gortesque & messy emergencies...learning the basics of Hyper Text Markup Language shouldn't be that tough!! Afterall the goal is to know enough so as to understand, manipulate and play around a little to get the results the way I have visualised it in my head. With all the help programmes in blogger.com and a few books it should be a cinch i.e with time ,experience and a little work :)",0,normal,blog_corpus,3740161.male.25.Science.Aries,,,,,,0
