"mood: bewildered I was driving home tonight from Chris's, and I listened to ""When You Come Back Down"" by Nickel Creek. Chris had played it earlier, but I didn't really listen to it. This time I did, and it made me cry a little, especially the line My greatest fear will be, that you will crash and burn, and I won't feel your fire and the line And I'll be on the other end, To hear you when you call, Angel, you were born to fly, If you get too high I'll catch you when you fall After that song I just shut off the radio and thought for the rest of my drive home. When I was almost home, I saw something go thru the sky for a brief second, then it disappeared. It couldn't have been a plane since it disappeared in mid air, then I realized it was a clear night, so it must have been a shooting star. I was kinda bewildered by it, but I took it as a song that everything is going to be ok, and kind of put my worries at ease a little. A little sign that I'm doing something right with everything. Well, it's time for bed.",0,normal,blog_corpus,747888.male.23.indUnk.Aries,,,,,,0
