"Today has been a good day. A problem that has already for long waited for some kind of a solution has finally been resolved. I’m not saying there won’t be any aftermath, but there’s at least some light in the end of the tunnel. So I’m happy, and a little proud of myself for making the first move. If you know me, you should realize it has not been easy. Now that I’ve gotten rid of the first issue, I have lots of negative feelings available waiting to be re-channeled. I’ve chosen my boss. How dare he chase me away from my working place! I remember one case study during University about some kind of a company where work was re-arranged so that no one had their own computer or working place any more. You’d come in the morning, take your pencil and stack of paper from your locker, grab a laptop from the secretary’s table and find a suitable place to sit, and they were not allowed to sit in the same place for two days in a row. I vaguely remember that this system proved to be not so good. If I remember correctly, it was discontinued quite soon after it was first introduced. So why doesn’t it work like that? Out of all people I should be the one who would not mind a change of scenery (three jobs within 12 months, think about it, and in the middle of it I took quite some time off to graduate from Uni), but I hate it as much as anyone would. Take for instance the polar-person sitting next to me today. She has a habit of keeping the window wide open even during sub-zero temperatures (luckily today it’s +8, I imagine it makes quite a difference). Last time I was here I tried to find some kind of a reasonable explanation for this phenomenon. Turns out she lives in an apartment where there’s no central heating, and be it for whatever reason, she only heats it herself every other day, even during winter. For those who are not familiar with the matter, some people heat theirs’ twice a day. Go figure then. The only consolation once again is what we northern people keep telling ourselves on the crispiest of winter days – oh no, it’s not unbelievably “freeze your ass off” cold outside, it’s simply refreshing, and it helps to keep us young for a longer time. Here’s to youth then!",0,normal,blog_corpus,2686446.female.24.Government.Taurus,,,,,,0
