"I went to New York on 11th to visit my very special friend. The weekend was spectacular. On Saturday we awoke to an ominous gray sky that promised to fill the concrete streets below with cold drops of unclean water. We decided to go have breakfast at a nearby diner. Midway through our meal, the clouds began to glide apart to reveal a vibrant and warm sun. Pale New Yorkers raided the streets of lower Manhattan to bask, crawl, dine, and shop. I've been suffering (gawd, I hate that word) from panic attacks and depression for the past 3 or 4 weeks. On Monday, I finally decided to go see a psychiatrist. She prescribed Zoloft and Xanax. They last time I was on Zoloft was last April. The psychiatrist had droopy boobs. I have to stay medicated for two years or so. Whomever runs this place gave me a lawn chair. Now I can sit out front with my rifle and shoot at Hoss when he tries to steal my shoes and my American flag.",0,normal,blog_corpus,908687.female.24.indUnk.Pisces,,,,,,0
