"The NeoCon ideology that is rife throughout the Pentagon and the many lies used to support its premises got us in to this shameful quagmire of a war in Iraq, now it turns out that those who duped the American public through lies and manipulations were they themselves duped by Iran, Ahmed Chalabi and the Iraqi National Congress. It seems that the INC was being run by Iran and was used for years to feed the US false information and to gather sensitive intelligence on what we were up to in the Middle East with regards to Iraq. In essence, the $340,000 per month we were paying Chalabi and his ragtag bunch of Iraqi ex-pats was really helping Iran fund it's intelligence operation against us! Touché Ayatollahs! The more we learn about what's really going on, the more it seems that this NeoCon cabal, which is the true ""power behind the throne"" at the Pentagon and in Washington, are all a bunch of misguided, power-hungry ideologues who apparently aren't too sharp. The Defense Intelligence Agency has concluded that a U.S.-funded arm of Ahmad Chalabi's Iraqi National Congress has been used for years by Iranian intelligence to pass disinformation to the United States and to collect highly sensitive American secrets, according to intelligence sources. ... Patrick Lang, former director of the intelligence agency's Middle East branch, said he had been told by colleagues in the intelligence community that Chalabi's U.S.-funded program to provide information about weapons of mass destruction and insurgents was effectively an Iranian intelligence operation. ""They [the Iranians] knew exactly what we were up to,"" he said.",0,normal,blog_corpus,1633534.male.39.Arts.Pisces,,,,,,0
"Cornerstone came and went. Time does fly when you're having fun - deas vail shows, watching other bands, great worship. Unfortunately when things weren't so fun, time was dragging along slow slow slow. David Crowder , Jason Morant , and Cool Hand Luke / Aireline / Anathallo all had awesome worship sets. The Pale actually put on the most surprising show. deas vail will be playing with them at Vino's next Saturday. Fans of OkGo and fun rock type stuff will like them alot. Mexico Mexico rocked it on the impromptu stage. I took a venture to the pit during a song. I borrowed a motorcycle helmet and bandana which both protected me from xkidsx. We played a few shows. One was on a stage about 8 feet in the air, it was weird, and really slippery. Unfortunately I lost my wallet on the way home in Missouri! We stopped at a gas station called Boomland in Benton, MO and I bought some food at McDonald's . So far no one has turned it in. I hope someone who needed some extra money found it. I only had about $80 in it but that could really help out someone who was starving or needed gas money. deas vail has a show this Saturday at a coffee shop in Ft. Smith. When I figure out more info. I'll post it asap. Kasey , thanks for the dedication. It took me a while to get through but I liked it. God bless you and your family.",0,normal,blog_corpus,4214747.male.23.indUnk.Taurus,,,,,,0
