"My subtle line wish-washed by Zorba's C-serum, I include the request for additional funding, equipment, such as the cannon shaped as a cuticle. The spectre mask on page eleven. The turpentine brassiere. When in girlhood I encountered the gilt edge of your plethora, Zorba put her hand to mast. Half-mast. She twisted the miniature dial and the tube rose, rose to meet my clapboard. Matched. At the end of the bath, read the bath leaves, the ring and the hollow skins of the bath beads. Even in the dank, we rinse the strawberry from our turbans, we frame the jaw with petrol. Curl it, Zorba. The tin tub waits, the lady, the tramp.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3553195.female.27.indUnk.Aries,,,,,,0
