"It was February 14th if I remember correctly. The world around me was completely and utterly gray. I remember waking up in my small apartment and checking myself in the mirror. I was whiter than usual. This wasnt of much notice yet. I cupped my hands to catch the water. As I was bringing it to my face I noticed a red line across my wrist. Again I put it aside for that today I was going to meet her. I splashed my face with the clear water. Again and again I did it. I looked up into the mirror and to my horror the clear water that was previously in my hands was now blood red and all over my face. I quickly dried my face and ran out of the room. I hurriedly put on my black coat and hat and left the apartment. Outside my door was a small envelope. I opened it to find printed on the piece of stationary the word boo. This was obviously a prank from Mr. and Mrs. Poes son. I put it in my pocket and went downstairs and out the door. Outside the world was an eerie gray hue. I remember seeing a family walking. The man was holding the book time machine and a travel guide. He tilted his hat at me and courteously I did the same. I crossed the street to begin my way through the park when a car came hurtling at me. Its headlights: red. I jumped out of the way in time. I lay there on the cold ground when a man leaned over me. Are you ok? he asked. Yes, yes Im fine I replied. He outstretched his hand offering a hoist up. Only there was no hand only the skeletal remains of one. I jumped up without his help and began to run through the park. I remember a little group of small girls all dressed in black singing ring around the rosy. I looked away then looked back to see a skeleton with a scythe in the middle of the ring. I ran faster still. My heart was pounding. I came to a playground and stopped for a rest for I saw no one there to harm me. I sat down on the bench to look upon my previous encounters and determine if they were real. Hello a sweet voice behind me said. I turned around to see another black clad girl. She held up her hand and in it was a wallet. I checked my back pocket realizing it was my own she was holding. I asked her to give it back but in response she turned and ran. Our chase brought us to the other end of the park and across the street. She turned into an alleyway. I entered it to. I saw her at the end holding open a door laughing. I ran to her but she went through the door. I stopped at it considering the consequences. (Obviously not enough). When I entered I found a long white hall. I walked to the end of it finding a door. I walked through into a room with metal walls. In the middle was a desk with a light on it, some paper, and there sat my wallet alongside a pen. I picked it up and turned to exit the room only to find there was no door at all. No exit. So here I sit at the desk, writing about my mornings events, waiting. There is a dripping noise coming from something unseen. So far I have counted about 630 drips. I think the light will go out soon. And there it goes. Im alone now. Good bye Lenore. Good bye.",0,normal,blog_corpus,730427.male.15.Arts.Capricorn,,,,,,0
