"Musicians as such are potently expressive with their music, their lyrics - instrumentation, et al. The visual side of things is almost wholly an outlet of ego, and the distinct lack of visual sophistication is especially evident in contrived band and artist photographs. There is a palpable difference between a shot of soulful involvement in performance and just standing with the band or hamming with an instrument. I enjoy the melodramatic exaggerated poses, the vast sweeping validity claim of standing with the gang, but does anyone else? The photograph represents such raw ego that it is almost funny. I say this first about myself, eh? So chill out. Now for those of you that like the written word, fear not. This is not going to be ONLY a PHOTOBLOG with brief captions. I am going to drag out all of my old publicity writing, press releases, band bios, music reviews, and all the detritus of a career failed not once, but several times. I just didn't get it soon enough. It's a waste of time pursuing a primarily western artform in a populous asian nation. They want group gyrations and tree-hugging, not guitar soloes. DUH! Well, it's photos for the first month at least. I'm gonna have to buy a scanner and ocr the other shyte. Enjoy, and don't laugh TOO hard. Blood sweat and tears went into all of this, and SOME of the people depicted herein are actually among the world's finest musicians. PS: Hello is hanging so it'll only be next week. Sorry. Sigh.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3515674.male.34.Telecommunications.Taurus,,,,,,0
"I can't be alone in the world wishing that Robert Winston would shut up. His recent outburst directed towards Prince Charles has just made me dislike him even more. I happen to think that Prince Charles is great at raising public and political awareness about issues. Let's face it, the man has a lot of time and resources at his disposal to enable him to actually research these areas that concern him and many others. Besides anybody who tries to make a bit of trouble for greedy politicians is alright by me. I know he gets it a bit wrong sometimes, but generally I think he's right to make people sit up and listen. In the Indie article he explains that it is nanoparticles that really concern him (and not robots) and I for one think he's right in asking for more research into the effects of such compounds. The effect of using nanoparticles in contact with the skin may be very different from ordinary sized particles. I think the point is here that we just don't know, and a real effort to reassure people with facts is required. Winston's and other people's reactions to Charle's opinion doesn't help the situation. This kind of attitude is precisely what makes people suspicious in the first place. Scientists must be able to justify what they do, and it mustn't be a case of ""we can do it, so we will do it""",0,normal,blog_corpus,1970542.female.24.indUnk.Gemini,,,,,,0
"The museum yesterday was fun, but, I was bummed that we didn't get to see the dinosaurs. Apparently there's a new exhibit under construction and it won't open until May, 2006. Boourns on that. You know, Too Much Light Makes the Baby Go Blind wasn't as good as I remember it being. It used to be 90% comedy skits, and 10% serious. But, now it's half serious skits, half comedy, and the comedy isn't as good :-/. I'm sorry to say it, but the current cast isn't as good as it was the first couple times I saw it. Holy shit, the taxi ride home was brutal. The dude did 80 mph the entire way home, and managed to scare the shit out of us. today, I woke up, showered, watched Sleepless in Seattle , ate cocoa pebbles, fell asleep, woke up, ate a burrito, tried to go bowling, didn't bowl, bought a garbage can, ate Thai food, came home, and played The Chronicles of Riddick: Escape From Butcher Bay for my Xbox . Holy crap, Riddick is a good game. Well, I've got a full 5 day work-week ahead of me. Apparently, we get July 5th off. Good times there, I guess. My buddy, Dan, is going to be coming back from Iraq this upcoming weekend. It'll be really fucking great to see him. it's been almost 6 months since he's been out, so, it's been awhile. His girlfriend, Molly, is super fucking excited about his return. He'll only be here for a couple weeks, but, I'm sure that they'll make the most of it. ah well. I'm gunna read for awhile, and try to get some zzzzzz's.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3003525.male.23.Technology.Gemini,,,,,,0
