"I was gone all day yesterday to go to a friend's birthday party. He decided to hold it at the Tokyo Diner. It was awesome! We decided to go with Hibachi (where they cook the food right in front of you). I jumped back when the chef made this huge wall of fire come up. ^_^; Then he did this thing that he called ""Mt. Fuji"" where he made an onion look like a little volcano. There was fire shooting up from it and everything. It was really funny when he tossed shrimp into our mouths because everybody missed. I also tried Miso soup (I think it was Miso soup...I'm not too sure what it was) and I liked it. The sushi (we got California rolls) was good. We played DDR the rest of the time (with a little Armored Core at the end). I also got a Spongebob necklace from my friends! ^_^ Then I played some more FF7 at home. I got to the scene where *SPOILER FOR THOSE OF YOU WHO HAVE NEVER PLAYED THIS* Aeris dies...it was so sad that I cried! I think the music was what made me cry the most. I still like Sephiroth, though. Speaking of Sephiroth, I finally beat him in Kingdom Hearts! He was tough, but I did it! ^_^",0,normal,blog_corpus,3507489.female.14.indUnk.Sagittarius,,,,,,0
