"So, here's what I've got so far. Black squirrels are either a variation or a melanistic shade of gray squirrel, so they can interbreed. The theory is that black squirrels are found mostly up north because their dark color gives them a slight edge in the cold winters, and are found near cities because their unusual color messes up their camoflauge. They are by no means typical, but not rare in northern WI. I was way off. I was guessing a camoflauge advantage. Ah well.",0,normal,blog_corpus,2229187.female.26.indUnk.Pisces,,,,,,0
