"Ah, screw. I hate it when I'm in deep thought and get all these weird and super thoughts... then I forget them before I get a chance to write them down. That's why I keep a journal. Not a diary, because I write down thought snippets, not ""this is what is happening in my life thus far"". Although you can probably call it a diary. [Is the period supposed to be inside the "" or outside? According to Lynne Truss the American way is to put it on the outside and the British way is to put it on the inside, and the American way doesn't make sense, just like everything else American, etc., etc., but I put it on the outside and I don't see why putting it on the inside makes sense. I mean, come on. Let's eat some of the cafeteria's ""hotdogs"". versus Let's eat some of the cafeteria's ""hotdogs."" Doesn't the first way make more sense? But maybe I'm biased. I probably am, considering I've been doing it the ""American way"" all my life. Well, most of my life, the parts I can remember, at any rate.] I am tired of my Great Search For A Nice-Looking Blog Skin. So I'll make do with this until I get a good one. THE PRINCESS BRIDE SPECIAL EDITION DVD is only 15 buckaroos. Hm. I feel very un-special. I want to dance and sing and be good at it. =( I am going to grow up to be an untalented all-I-can-do-is-study-and-work-and-stress person. Boo. [Where is Kalamazoo?]",0,normal,blog_corpus,1748233.female.15.Non-Profit.Pisces,,,,,,0
"Ahh, another weekend half over as I sit up late wasting time on computers. Life has been grand lately. Had a bday, seen Pips over the weekend and generally had a great time just living life with Nats. I have to say that I'm not where I thought I would be right now. Working harder than I ever have seems oddly challenging and satisfying in a way even though I know it is slowly sucking my will to live. So many people I work with are ""Go-getters"" the brightest and hard working of the bunch. It makes life a living hell working with people who never slack off, it means I can't. Bygones. I know sometimes life is not the best it could be but by god I am happy to be alive and living free. I am in debt, not happy with my job, and battling a cursed sore on my foot but huzzah happiness is a drug in itself. I know life is so hard in so many different ways for people but living it the best I can is all I can do. Man, we went down to ole Mifflin street for a Mad town block party today for pure craziness. Met Pips and Mary down at a house party. The block party was 3 blocks of house parties with 50k people crammed into the street and lawns drinking, hell it's probably still going on. It baffles me how a regions attitudes can affect overarching attitudes. This kind of thing would never go over in champaign. I mean 50,000 people drinking in an insanely crowded area with cops? People would be fighting and rioting in seconds, maybe its not bad as I think but Wisconsin seems to be made of a calmer brand of people who are more tolerant and liberal. Sure cops were arresting people at the block party but in a calm fashion and not without due reason. Cliche of the day: changes in latitudes, changes in attitudes. Rock over Madison, where the mendota is so fine they named a lake after it. k.e.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3057571.male.23.indUnk.Taurus,,,,,,0
