"Press release; Jessie Shen, DigiTimes.com [Friday 6 August 2004] Lite-On Semiconductor (already merged with Dyna Image), a Taiwan-based manufacturer of image sensors, announced record high revenues of NT$841.82 million in July, up 9.7% on-month and 45.9% on-year. The accumulated revenues from January to July generated about NT$4.753 billion, up 42.3% on-year. In addition to its major products, including contact image sensors (CISs), CMOS image sensors and discrete components, the company secured new orders for its new compact camera module (CCM) product, which adopts a COB (chip-on-board) process, in June, according to the company. The company began listing on the Taiwan Stock Exchange (TSE) on July 19 this year. Lite-On: January-July revenues by segment (NT$m) Segment Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Image sensor 293 333 341 363 406 446 510 Discrete 268 260 277 294 309 321 332 Total 561 593 618 657 715 767 842 Source: company, compiled by DigiTimes, August 2004.",0,normal,blog_corpus,4151409.male.25.Engineering.Cancer,,,,,,0
