"George Foreman markets a grill. I bought that grill. What a happy man I am! I had left this grill sitting unused next to my stove for two weeks. This morning, I decided I did not want to buy any more fast food, and I took a small risk. I plugged in the machine, pulled a burger patty out of my freezer, and slapped it down on the grill. I was certain nothing could be so foolproof, let alone Hollando-proof. How wrong I was! Three grilled meals later, I am in full pseudo-Atkins mode, with nothing but meat, cheese, and spinach salads in my immediate future. I say ""pseudo-Atkins"" because I have no idea what constitutes an acceptable meal plan under the late doctor's regimen. Like the majority of other shoppers, I flip packages around to see which products have the fewest carbohydrates. I hope to do some research on the South Beach Diet after the Bar Exam. For now, though, this quaint little gadget is saving me from spending the same time, more money, and far more patience in the pursuit of not-so-fast food. Some would say it's healthier, too. Here is something my friends never thought I would say: ""Do you have any recipe ideas?"" Well, do you? Let me know...",0,normal,blog_corpus,3402054.male.26.Student.Virgo,,,,,,0
"I'm such a dipshit sometimes. Last night I went out with my sister and her boyfriend. We all had fun, but I had one too many drinks. I wasn't blasted out of my gourd, but I wasn't in any shape to drive. Anyway, we get back to the house and I proceed to call my...I guess you can call him friend or a friend with benefits. Whatever. Well I call him and we get into this big discussion about our relationship and how the distance is keeping us from being more than friends, blah, blah, blah. Well he says something that sets me off. Don't ask me what cuz I don't remember, but what I do recall, albeit somewhat fuzzy, I basically made an ass out of myself. Now, Mike doesn't realize how drunk I was. The conversation, from what I recollect and from what I have been able to glean from subsequent conversations, was not a disaster. More came out than either one of us was ready to deal with or wanted to deal with for that matter. But shit was laid out there and I hate that I don't really know what exactly was said. That pisses me off. I hate when I do that, but I don't seem to stop. I don't drink nearly as much as I did in my college days and I have been better about having diarrhea of the mouth when I have too many Jack and Cokes. I just want to have a better handle on my emotions and how and when to express them. I make things more complicated in every relationship I have ever been in with stupid stuff like this. I don't need alcohol to get myself on the dance floor so why am I completely honest only when I'm inebriated? Sober, I say what I think myself or the other person wants to hear. In the end I'm only being dishonest with myself and I screw up good healthy relationships. I know all of this in my head but I can't seem to convey it all the time. The really weird part is that when I don't tell half-truths or play a game of semantics things are better and the stress is not there to keep up that facade. So an intelligent person would see this and say ""Gee, I should do this all the time"". But noooooo, I have to be an idiot and fuck shit up. I want to cure this disease soon. I don't want my little girl to have to grow up guessing if what Mommy said is really true and if she should trust me. God, how do you expect any adolescent to listen to you and obey you if they know you are a crock of shit?! Chiara came along at a good time. She has accelerated my personal growth process in these last 3 years. Damn, if it wasn't for her, I'd be a more of a mess than I am now. I've heard that children can be the best teachers. Think about it for a second. An infant can teach you more about the joy or pure, unadulterated love than any other relationship can. They have just come from God himself. They are the closest we will ever get to experiencing the love God has for us in this world. Maybe that's why I melt when I hold a newborn. Maybe that's why my world slows and the dust settles leaving what is important clearly visible.",0,normal,blog_corpus,4106280.female.25.Construction.Aries,,,,,,0
