"Video Games Info?&nbsp; Got it the hard way. &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Well, it's good to be back.&nbsp; I realize that I lacked posting as a Video gaming correspondant, mainly because of the lack of released info since E3, but after many months of digging, I finally found a little more detail for upcoming games. &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Let's start with a recap on the Nintendo DS (and note that I don't fathom about Nintendo, they just seem to be the most popular):&nbsp; Dual Screens, both backlit, pushing 2-D and 3-D graphics that will actually exceed the quality of N-64 (most of which will operate with a 3-D person view and a 2-D map view); Touch Control which can be demonstrated on WarioWare, Inc. DS and Bandai's Mobile Suit Gundam Seed.&nbsp; WarioWare, you can use the stylus to play games that require you to rub on the screen until a picture appears underneath the streaks.&nbsp; Gundam Seed, you can use the stylus for targeting operations and jabbing enemies.&nbsp; This won't do away with buttons, but will allow a new connection with you and the game; Worldwide wireless connections:&nbsp; Just as a starter, you can connect with up to 16 people in a 30 ft range, but, &nbsp;it will also be WiFi compatible so that you can go to&nbsp;a Hub, such as a cyber cafe, and connect with people across the nation, or even globe!&nbsp; Nintendo has dubbed it their ""Third Pillar"" because of the amazing new softwares that they were never able to create before. Prices have also been determined.&nbsp; As a pre-order, the Nintendo DS ranges anywhere from 189.98 to 209.98. &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Now let's move on to the games.&nbsp; Metroid fans have been drooling over Metroid Prime 2: Echoes.&nbsp; Well, here's some more details: Guess what?&nbsp; If you liked fighting yourself in Metroid Fusion, here we go again.&nbsp; Samus will be traveling between two world now:&nbsp; The Light World of the Luminoth, and The Dark Wold of the Ing.&nbsp; Because of this, you will have two new beam weapons, each aiding you for each environment:&nbsp; The Light and Dark Beams.&nbsp; As you can guess, enemies in the Dark World tend to be damaged more by the Light Beam or grow from the Dark beam, and vice versa.&nbsp; Dark Samus will be an exceptional challenge, especially since it will be the first real boss that will not be bigger than you.&nbsp; Oh, and a Metroid first?&nbsp; 4 person multiplayer!&nbsp; More?&nbsp; How about the new Hacker upgrade for it?&nbsp; It allows you to, as Nintendo put it, ""upload a virus to competitors"" that will disable their suits, shut off their beams or limit them to Morph Ball form.&nbsp; Truly amazing.&nbsp; Oh, and for those of you who feel your GBA is too dear to you (or you just can't afford the DS), wireless attachtments will be available for GBA September 7th.&nbsp; Nintendo and Bandai have announced the development of wireless GBA games.&nbsp; As to whether or not DS wireless connections will be compatible with GBA, I have no information, but it more than likely will be as long as both systems have the same Pak.&nbsp; Also, Yu-Gi-Oh! and Dragonball GT has been announced for GBA Videos!&nbsp; Wireless Messenger will be made for the GBA also!&nbsp; Again, I'm not sure whether or not it will be compatible with a DS connection, but it most likely will. &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Here are some of the upcoming titles: Mario Kart DS, Animal Crossing DS, Pac-Pix, Pac 'N Roll, a Sonic DS (Title not yet made), Yu-Gi-Oh!: Nightmare Troubadour, Bomberman, Egg Monster Heroes, Mobile Suit Gundam Seed, Metroid Prime 2: Echoes, Resident Evil 4, Star Fox, Geist, Paper Mario 2, Donkey Konga, Pikmin 2, Advance Wars: Under Fire, Donkey Kong Jungle Beat, Odama, Viewtiful Joe 2, Prince of Persia 2, Def Jam: Fight for NY, Need for Speed: Underground 2, Tony Hawk's Underground 2: World Destruction Tour, King Arthur, Catwoman, The Lord of the Rings:&nbsp;The Third Age (GCN), Second Sight, Timesplitters:&nbsp;Future Perfect, Starcraft: Ghost, Tom Clancy's Splinter Cell: Pandora Tomorrow, Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon 2, Call of Duty: Finest Hour, Tak 2: The Staff of Dreams, Amazing Island, Dead Rush, Goldeneye: Rogue Agent, The Legend of Zelda: The Minish Cap, Pokemon Firered and Leafgreen, F-Zero:&nbsp;GP Legend, Mario Pinball, Donkey Kong Country 2, DK: King of Swing, Kirby & The Amazing Mirror, Kingdom Hearts: Chain of Memories, Nicktoons, Cartoon Network Block Party, Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles, Gundam Seed:&nbsp;Battle Assault, Astro Boy: Omega Factor, Megaman Zero 3, Racing Gears Advance, Madden NFL 2005, Banjo Pilot, The Lord of the Rings: The Third Age (GBA), Boktai 2: Solar Boy Django, and Tron 2.0.&nbsp; So, as you can see, the industry will be hard at work this year making some awesome games (most of the anyway). &nbsp; Expressing my love for Anime?&nbsp; Looks like it's going the hard way. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Well, I'm working on Installation 2 of my series, for those who have read the first one (again, the address is http://codelyokostories.cjb.net under Code: Lyoko-Chaos Factor) and have made it to Chapter 4.&nbsp; I still am not sure how long it will be exactly, but it will at least have 6 Chapters.&nbsp; Questions, comments, custom character submissions, or suggestions?&nbsp; Please send me an email or register at the Lyoko Network forums and send me a Personal Message (PM). &nbsp;",0,normal,blog_corpus,1131329.male.13.indUnk.Leo,,,,,,0
