"1. I don't remember Mr. Noel, high school political science teacher. I do, however, remember Mr. Noel senior outing chaperone. While on said senior outing, he told Whitey: ""No one likes you, Bob, and you have no friends."" That was a) totally rich and b) said when Bob was surrounded by all of his friends. 2. Today is my last day in Denver. I return to Chi tomorrow, will be in Champaign on Thursday and Friday nights, and then leave for Philly on Sunday. 3. Now, onto the currently completely impractical race around the world. I have several objections. First, the budget is WAYYY too low. This can be rectified by adding in a provision that you can work---ala Alexander Supertramp aka Chris McCandless-- to finance your journey during the journey. However, different people in the race will have different marketable skills. For example, Joel will be skilled at talking about hardcore metal or whatever, Whitey will be skilled at male prostitution, and I will be skilled at being an upstanding young citizen. SO...we must limit the type of work one can engage in. I propose that that race participants (hereafter ""racers"" ) can only work as ditchdiggers. As ditchdiggers, racers must earn their keep doing one thing, and one thing only: Digging those fucking ditches. It is perfect for the around the world race (ATWR) because it tests diligence, intestinal fortitude, and lots of other shit. It will also pad your pocketbook. Even assuming that racers do not pay for lodging, we still have to pay for our sustenance. This will require more than 1000 USD each, especially when I'm on the Cambodian/ Laos border where rice costs approximately .00001 cents per bag, but I can't find any motherfucking soy sauce. But I hear they have a booming ditchdigging market in Phenom Penh. 4. As Stick would say, I stonebutt and render your latitude longitude requirements usless, pursuant to point six (6) of my revisions to your original proposal 5. OBVIOUSLY no one can take planes or helicopters. However, I have a few caveats. a) if a racer makes enough money digging ditches to buy his/ her own plane, he/ she can do so and fly in it, with the express provision that he/ she is a licsensed pilot and flies the plane. b) Racers can travel via air in a hot air balloon, but only if it's with Steve Fossett c) Racers can travel by zeppelin any time they so choose. 6. I think that there must be some checkpoints in the ATWR. For example, one checkpoint could be a Norwegian fjord. Another could be Everest Base Camp. Or another could be Mr. Lessek's Hilton Head House. This would engender a healthy competition within the race, thereby keeping racers interested and not focused on lucrative ditchdigging work. 7. I can't wait for Joel to blog on how my ideas suck, and how his original race proposal was dead sexy. 8. Joel, we will talk about the ATWR more when I am down in Champaign on Thursday/ Friday. 9. I obviously will win this race.",0,normal,blog_corpus,3877004.male.25.indUnk.Capricorn,,,,,,0
