"Jack from NYC called me last night and planned to come to Nashville today. I don't want to blow him off on the phone and also tried to give me a chance to know someone who might be interesting in person although he is awefully full of himself on the phone. As planned, he arrived Nashville around 12 at noon. I got up not long before that. It was a good 8 hour sleep although it took me long time to go to sleep due to the strong caffine from Starbucks. I guided him to Borders bookstore and as he approached me, he looked a lot older than his picture appeared on the website. Anyway, his age and appearance has nothing to do my little intersest in him. All I have agreed before hand is to meet him. I tried to know him better with an open heart. We headed towards P. F. Chang right afterwards and had lunch together. The cantonese duck is DIVINE, well, at least in the U.S.A. considering I haven't had that for a LONG time. The initial converstation went okay. He then became more full of himself and talked on and on about how successful his career is and how he can get free flight and free hotel stays, plus free prescription drugs from the greatest Pfizer he worked form. I have great respect for his success and his lifestyle. It's just not cool to brag about it for hours. I felt sorry for him. Another reason I don't like him is he tends to be very aggressive sexually. I mean it's a good thing is he know me well. However, he just met men and started groping all over and feel my muscles. That's so not cool. I got enough of him and just wanted him to leave around 5:30pm. I'm so glad Huawei came back home around 6 and he decided it was time for him to jet. I tried to be very nice with his leave and hoped never see him again. Hope this poor guy could grow up a little bit before he crash his next date. :)",0,normal,blog_corpus,1764916.male.24.Engineering.Sagittarius,,,,,,0
