"How do you break up with your b/f when he wants to marry you, but you want to be single and enjoy your single life while you can? Just tell him exactly that. Sure it's going to hurt him, it would hurt anyone. Guys usually admire honesty and like it when you are straightforward. Unfortunately girls will a lot of times be wishy-washy and try to do things with subtletly. And just as unfortunate, guys don't catch on to your subtle things and innuendo. Also I have witnessed many times where one partner wants to break it off but doesn't have the guts to do it. So they try (badly) to get the other person to break up with them. DON'T DO THIS! People usually think that if the other person breaks it off then it's not THEIR OWN fault that the relationship ended and all of the world will take pity on them because they got dumped. Problem with this method is that it usually involves doing bad things in the first place to get the other person to dump you and then just hoping they get fed up with you and decide to end it. So just give it to him straight and if you are right for each other then you can get back together in a few years or whatever. If it's not right and it's not going to be, don't drag him along anymore. He's going to want to enjoy his single life too.",0,normal,blog_corpus,798653.male.26.indUnk.Aquarius,,,,,,0
